    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7973": {
      "title": "Hartford Art School Operations Manager",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Hartford Art School Operations Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Hartford Art School Operations Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Hartford Art School Operations Manager FLSA Classification EX Reports to Dean, Hartford Art School Salary Range F Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week Monday - Friday with some nights and weekends Position Summary Oversees daily office and facility operations, faculty needs, student services, and supply management for the Hartford Art School. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range The budgeted starting salary for this position is $50,455 to $58,000 Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Oversees and manages day-to-day facilities operations and identifies maintenance needs. Works with University Facilities department and outside vendors to ensure the timely completion of minor facility repairs, upgrades, and improvement projects. Purchases supplies, equipment and contracts labor as required. Supervises and coordinates the work of all HAS technical staff. Coordinates the hiring, onboarding, training, and scheduling of HAS technicians and student workers including scheduling and time reporting. Coordinates, schedules, and creates contract for live studio models. Acts as College liaison with Facilities and outside vendors on maintenance and construction projects. Monitors building conditions and ensuring studios, classrooms, shops, and common areas are safe, functional, and well-maintained. Partners with faculty to monitor, track, and coordinate the purchase of course supplies and expenditures related to student course work. Manages inventory of equipment, tools, and consumable materials for the College. Assists with space planning, studio setup, and special events requiring facility support. Supports compliance with all safety protocols, equipment maintenance schedules, and regulatory requirements. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with the Facilities Department and external vendors to schedule equipment and facility maintenance and to ensure proper clean-up of departmental spaces. Enforces facility access policies for students and faculty. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1244P Working Conditions Normal Office situation Requires travel, excluding overnight stays Stockroom or warehouse High dust, dirt, grease environment Requires safety training and/or protective devices Requires exposure to moving machinery and/or vehicles Works with poor ventilation or with regular exposure to odors Regular exposure to chemicals and solvents Education Bachelor Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table Intermittently sitting, standing, stooping Typically standing and/or walking Occasional pushing and/or pulling Occasional heavy lifting or carrying 51 lbs. or more Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7968 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue West Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
