    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7877": {
      "title": "Manager of Student Services and Evaluation",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Manager of Student Services and Evaluation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Manager of Student Services and Evaluation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Manager of Student Services and Evaluation FLSA Classification NE Reports to Assistant Director, Undergraduate Academic Services and Enrollment Compliance Salary Range G1 Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for the support of student academic progress through the Office of the Registrar, primarily through technical and functional use the University’s databases of record. Responsible for updating student records, performing degree evaluations, and awarding of student degrees in assigned college. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range $20 to $21.50 per hour Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Manages student academic progress in Degree Works. Supports the Assistant Registrar in their work managing Degree Works, including assisting with upgrades, testing, data reporting and training. Also collaborates with the Assistant Registrar in identifying areas for improvement for services within the scope of responsibility, which may include new approaches and processes that help promote efficiencies for the Office of the Registrar and University. Serves as a liaison between students and department heads to resolve academic discrepancies, deficiencies in student progress, potential corrective measures and other academic issues as necessary and/or appropriate. Evaluates student academic records. Updates transfer credits into Banner, per college determination. Reviews and/or updates records and related student information used for enrollment, academic statistics, programs and/or scholarship. Assists in the development and implementation of procedures and forms regarding students. Manages multiple priorities under established time constraints. Handles highly sensitive information with confidentiality and tact. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with various internal and external constituencies. Supports Registrar personnel as needed, in one or more of the following areas, scheduling, commencement, Acalog, academic reporting. Maintains departmental files that are accurate and in compliance with record keeping policies. Also files student academic program data to ensure the integrity of the database in compliance with established policies as well as data integrity standards. Represents the Office of the Registrar on committees as necessary and appropriate. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1224P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Bachelor’s Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Light lifting or carrying 25 lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7860 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Requi