    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7967": {
      "title": "Dance Education Outreach Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Dance Education Outreach Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Dance Education Outreach Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Dance Education Outreach Coordinator FLSA Classification EX Reports to Director, Hartt Community Division Salary Range G Weeks Per Year 44 Work Week Monday - Friday with some nights and weekends Position Summary Assumes responsibility as administrative leader of The Hartt Community Division ( HCD ) dance programs, including oversight of all aspects of the academic year dance outreach activities and performances. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s HCD students. Hiring Range The budgeted starting salary for this 10 month position will be $45,000 Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Provides leadership in the administration, staffing, supervision and teaching for HCD dance outreach programs and specific staff to ensure they meet the mission of the HCD as well as The Hartt School. Manages all aspects of both off-campus and satellite/outreach operations of the HCD dance programs. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with satellite school/outreach coordinators in public and private schools as well as community organizations. Pursues grant opportunities and establish new community relationships Works with Dance Booster group in conjunction with Director of Dance Programs Co-produces Harttworks production and coordinate other academic year and summer dance productions Develops, reviews and proposes all HCD outreach dance program budgets in consultation with the Director of Dance Programs and the HCD Assistant Director of Finance . Handles highly sensitive information with confidentiality and tact. Manages the HCD outreach dance programs within the framework of an approved balanced budget. Collaborates with the Director of HCD in the development of policies, procedures and written correspondence which aid in the management of all HCD activities and programs. Collaborates with the HCD Registrar/Data Manager to maintain HCD’s data management system to ensure the integrity of the data. Collaborates with HCD staff on Dance Department marketing strategy. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1243P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Requires travel, including overnight stays Education Bachelor’s degree required (or equivalent experience for dance faculty) Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Light lifting or carrying 25 lbs. or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7966 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
