    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7976": {
      "title": "Gallery Preparator and Registrar",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Gallery Preparator and Registrar Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Gallery Preparator and Registrar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Gallery Preparator and Registrar FLSA Classification NE Reports to Gallery Director/Curator Salary Range G1 Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assists the Gallery Director and assumes responsibility for the daily management and preparator role of the Joseloff and Silpe Galleries, in addition to the Kaman Print Study Center, to ensure successful exhibitions and programming. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range The budgeted salary for this position will be 37.5 hours at $20.00 to $21.00 per hour dependent upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Receives and sends artwork and relevant gallery materials. Installs and de-installs artwork. Prepares wall and spaces including patching and painting walls and pedestals. Responsible for manager gallery materials stocked and organized. Organizes the art collection and digital database Handles on-campus loans from the collection. Ensures correct and current didactic and label information is installed in a timely manner. Facilitates and coordinates with campus partners and external contractors for maintaining and cleaning gallery spaces, gallery preparation, printing, and other services. Hires, trains, schedules, and manages student gallery monitors. Ensures Front Desk is always staffed; covers as required. Responsible for reserving on-campus spaces for programming, including visiting artist lectures. Coordinates with on-site catering for reception needs. Submits gallery event information to on-campus and off-campus digital spaces. Schedules and hosts class visits and tours. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1240P Working Conditions Normal Office Situation Requires travel, excluding overnight stays. Stockroom or warehouse High dust, dirt, grease environment Works with poor ventilation or with regular exposure to odors Education Bachelor’s Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at desk or table Intermittently sitting, stand, stooping Typically standing and/or walking Typically crawling and/or kneeling Typically pushing and/or pulling Requires repeated reaching by extending hand(s) and/or arm(s) in any direction Heavy lifting or carrying 51 pounds or more Climbing ladders or scaffolds Using equipment requiring high dexterity Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Occasional attendance for events after business hours is required. Previous gallery and preparator management experience is preferred. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7960 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue West Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7989": {
      "title": "Director of Student Onboarding & Success",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Director of Student Onboarding &amp; Success Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Student Onboarding & Success Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Student Onboarding & Success FLSA Classification EX Reports to Dean of Students and Associate Vice President for Student Experience Salary Range D Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week Monday - Friday with some nights and weekends Position Summary Provides strategic leadership for the University’s comprehensive new-student experience, guiding students from admission deposit through the completion of their second academic year. Develops, coordinates, and assesses initiatives that support enrollment conversion, successful changeovers, engagement, belonging, and retention. Leads new student orientation, changeover programming, first-year experience initiatives, and second-year success efforts, working closely with the parent and family engagement personnel and academic and student affairs partners to create a seamless student journey. Using institutional data, the identifies students who could benefit from additional support during academic, social, and personal changes, develops targeted interventions, and continuously improves programming to increase orientation participation, yield, student success, and retention. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s goals and mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range Budged starting salary is $66,750 to $77,000, depending upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership Develops and leads the University’s comprehensive onboarding strategy from deposit through the end of the second year. Establishes measurable goals aligned with enrollment, student success, and retention priorities. Leads institutional planning for new-student transitions in partnership with academic and student affairs leadership. Onboarding & Orientation Programs Leads First-Year Orientation, Transfer Orientation, Family Orientation, Opening Weekend, and Winter Orientation. Recruits, trains, and supervises the Orientation Leader program and student staff team. Chairs the Onboarding Committee, coordinating representatives from Admissions, Advising, Registrar, Student Financial Services, Residence Life, Accessibility, Health Services, Public Safety, and Enrollment. Transition & Retention Programming Develops and leads First Six Weeks and Weeks of Welcome programming to sustain engagement after orientation. Designs catch-up pathways for students who miss orientation, mid-year entrants, and transfer students. Develops Sophomore Success initiatives, including a sophomore retreat, involvement and leadership pathways, and re-engagement outreach for at-risk second-year students. Data-Informed Retention Management Monitors orientation registration and attendance in real time; identify no-shows within 24 hours and coordinate immediate outreach. Establishes and tracks attendance as a formal KPI , distinct from registration. Tracks first-year and second-year persistence by orientation participation status and recommend interventions. Produces an annual report on orientation attendance, yield conversion, satisfaction, and retention outcomes. Partnerships Coordinates consistently with Admissions, Academic Advising, Residence Life, Student Engagement, Accessibility, Financial Aid, Health Services, Public Safety, Faculty, Marketing, and Enrollment Management. Supervisory Responsibility Chairs the Onboarding Committee; directly supervises Orientation Leaders, Returning Student Mentors (Red Caps), and a Graduate Assistant (if available). Performs other duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1249P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Master’s Degree required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Light lifting or carrying, 25lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/7988 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8017": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Sport Management (2027 2028)",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant Professor Sport Management (2027 2028) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Tenure Track Assistant Professor Sport Management (2027 2028) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Tenure Track Assistant Professor Sport Management (2027 2028) Rank Assistant Professor Salary Range $112,000 Tenure Information Tenure Track Job Description The Barney School of Business at the University of Hartford is seeking to fill a tenure-track assistant professor position in Sport Management beginning August 2027. Responsibilities The successful applicant will ordinarily teach courses in Sport Management and related business disciplines on-site and online in undergraduate and graduate programs. The typical teaching load is four courses per semester. Specific responsibilities may change based on departmental needs. The Assistant Professor of Sport Management is expected to sustain an active scholarly research agenda with peer-reviewed publications and presentations at relevant conferences to maintain the AACSB Scholarly Academic qualification and to make progress toward successful tenure and promotion. The faculty member will also be expected to participate in department, college, and university level committees. The Assistant Professor will serve as an advisor to students guiding them in courses and career-development. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to inclusive excellence, which the University defines as an unwavering commitment to fostering a vibrant campus community where every student, staff member, and faculty colleague feels deeply rooted, empowered to flourish, and inspired to achieve their highest potential. Required Qualifications Required: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in Sport Management, Sport Administration, a business discipline with a Sport Management concentration, or closely related area. ABD candidates with documentation of degree completion prior to September 2027 will be considered. Preferred: Applicants should: be able to teach a wide variety of sport management and business courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels both on-site and online. demonstrate evidence of quality scholarly activities demonstrate strong teaching ability and communication skills. show evidence of incorporating appropriate technology in teaching. show commitment to inclusive excellence and belonging. Preferred Qualifications Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Teaching Philosophy Statement of Inclusive Excellence As an institution of higher learning, the University of Hartford strives to be more than merely a mirror of the larger society; it should foster learning and encourage the personal growth of students, faculty, and staff in an environment that promotes and celebrates diversity in all of its forms regardless of identifying factors including but not limited to race, sex, age, religion, national origin, socioeconomic status, physical and learning differences, sexual orientation, gender or gender identity. Accordingly, our commitment is to: · Foster an inclusive, equitable, just, and caring community where the unique identities of each person are fully appreciated, respected, and celebrated · Engage in civil discourse, that values diverse intellectual perspectives · Cultivate a campus community reflective of the intersectionality of the larger society while maintaining an environment of safety and respect where all members experience a sense of belonging · Institutionally, stand against acts of hate, intimidation, discrimination, bigotry, violence, and harassment of any kind · Uphold the values of the institution, so that all our members are treated with dignity and respect Our commitment to Inclusive Excellence and Belonging is a strength that results in a vibrant and more engaged campus culture. Teaching Philosophy In the teaching philosophy statement, please share your thoughts and experiences in using active learning strategies, high-impact practices, and evidence-based pedagogical practices, as well as your methods for engaging students and fostering student belonging in the classroom. University Information Students at the University of Hartford find success in a learning environment that both challenges and mentors them. Our academic mission is to engage students in acquiring the knowledge, skills, and values necessary to thrive in, and contribute to, a pluralistic, complex world. At the University of Hartford, we are committed to community. We are an academic community that values integrity, curiosity, creativity, excellence, responsibility, and accomplishment. Enriched by our engagement with, and understanding of, one another, we take pride in our shared traditions and experiences. We are dedicated to building a culture that respects all of its members and celebrates their contributions as we work together to strengthen our community. The full text of our academic mission, vision, and values can be seen at www.hartford.edu. Opportunities for faculty development and support can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/campus-leadership/office-provost/faculty-development/ and a listing of Affinity Networks can be found at https://www.hartford.edu/about/diversity-inclusion/affinity-groups.aspx College Information The Barney School of Business is nationally ranked by Bloomberg Businessweek (undergraduate), U.S. News and World Report ( MBA ) and Princeton Review (overall business school). The Barney School of Business enrolls over 1,000 students in nine undergraduate majors, fourteen undergraduate minors, and four graduate programs. The programs are accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business ( AACSB ), a designation given to the top 6% of business schools globally. The mission of the Barney School of Business is to cultivate and inspire intellectually curious learners to be competent, confident, and connected. Through our programs, we create an authentic learning experience that empowers learners to become effective business leaders. We invest in our faculty and staff and provide opportunities to expand their professional development. More information on the school and its mission can be found at http://www.hartford.edu/barney Posting Detail Information Posting Number F222P Open Date 10/19/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently or have you ever been a part-time faculty member at the University of Hartford? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Teaching Portfolio Optional Documents 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8024": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, Athletics and Recreation",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Executive Assistant, Athletics and Recreation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Executive Assistant, Athletics and Recreation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Executive Assistant, Athletics and Recreation FLSA Classification NE Reports to Assistant Vice President for Athletics and Recreation Salary Range G1 Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 35 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for providing executive, administrative and analytical support to the Dean/Director/Department Head, proactively undertaking initiatives to enhance the quality and utility of materials and activities as well as the effective operations of the office. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range Budgeted Salary is $20 per hour to $25.50 per hour, depending upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with both internal and external constituencies, providing executive, administrative and analytical support in short- and long-range strategic planning initiatives for the department/college as well as to ensure timely and effective communications between and among internal and external constituents. Monitors and controls the calendar and time commitments of the Dean/Director/Department Head, evaluating and prioritizing requested meetings and managing complex schedules to accommodate needs. Screens all incoming calls and correspondence to the Office, providing assistance and a welcoming presence to visitors to the Office. Serves as a project manager for assigned tasks, keeping the Dean/Director/Department Head informed on the status of the project. Serves as the centralized point for operational expenditures, grants and/or personnel transactions within the department/college. Develops, audits and oversees budget expenditures, providing reports to the Dean/Director/Department Head in an effort to ensure prudent fiscal management. Maintains supporting files and documentation to ensure the integrity of the information. Prepares agendas, records and distributes minutes as necessary and/or appropriate. Acts as a primary liaison for all staff that support the Dean/Director/Department Head, providing oversight on initiatives to be taken on the Dean’s behalf in compliance with established institutional deadlines. Drafts internal and external correspondence for signature as necessary and/or appropriate. Researches and prepares reports as requested. Maintains accurate and complete administrative records to ensure the integrity of the database in compliance with established policies as well as data integrity standards. Assists in the development and dissemination of departmental policies and procedures. Actively participates in the analysis, recommendation and implementation of business process improvement efforts to ensure the proper use of technology and improve operational effectiveness as necessary and/or appropriate. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1258P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Bachelor’s Degree preferred. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Intermittently sitting, standing, stooping. Light lifting or carrying, 25lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8023 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8022": {
      "title": "Senior Resident Director",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Senior Resident Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Senior Resident Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Senior Resident Director FLSA Classification EX Reports to Associate Director, Residential Education & Community Development Salary Range G Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum); may nights and weekends as needed. Position Summary Manages an assigned residential community while providing department-wide leadership in designated areas of Residential Education. Serves as a lead practitioner and peer resource for the Resident Director team, helping coordinate departmental processes, staff development, training, and implementation of residential education priorities. Support Residential Life Leadership team by providing day-to-day coordination, mentoring, and leadership for designated departmental initiatives. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. As a live-in position, responsibilities include evening, nighttime and weekend commitments on a regular basis throughout the academic year, including time reserved for preparatory training. In addition, the campus residency shall serve as their primary residence. Hiring Range $46785, plus room/board Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities Residential Community Leadership Manages an assigned residential community and provides visible, accessible leadership to residents. Supervises, coaches, evaluates, and develops assigned Resident Assistants and/or graduate staff. Implements the University’s residential curriculum and community-development expectations. Develops strategies that promote student belonging, engagement, responsibility, well-being, and academic success. Responds to student concerns and facilitates appropriate referrals to University resources. Supports community standards and addresses behavioral concerns consistent with University policies. RD Team Leadership & Coordination Serves as a senior peer resource and mentor to Resident Directors, particularly newer professional staff. Assists the Associate Director with coordination of departmental priorities and consistent implementation across residential communities. Facilitates RD meetings, training sessions, or working groups when assigned. Helps identify operational challenges, recurring student concerns, and opportunities for improvement and communicates them to the Associate Director. Provides leadership during major departmental periods including staff training, opening, closing, RA selection, and transition periods. May provide short-term coverage or coordination when another RD position is vacant. Departmental Functional Portfolio Maintains leadership responsibility for one or more significant departmental functions as assigned based on institutional priorities and staff expertise. Portfolios may include: RA recruitment and selection RA training and professional development Residential curriculum and programming First-Year Residential Experience Continuing/Upper-Level Student Experience Student leadership Assessment and student feedback Staff recognition and engagement Opening/closing coordination Develops annual goals for assigned portfolios, coordinates implementation across residential communities, and reports outcomes to the Associate Director. Staff Training & Development Assists with development and implementation of RA and professional staff training. Provides coaching and resources to RDs regarding supervision, programming, community development, and student concerns. Helps establish consistent expectations and practices across residential communities. Supports onboarding and mentoring of newly hired Resident Directors. Crisis Response & Duty Participates in the professional staff on-call rotation. Responds to residential emergencies, student crises, facilities concerns, and significant incidents. Serves as an experienced resource to RDs and RAs during complex incidents while appropriately escalating significant matters to the Associate Director. Coordinates with Public Safety, Counseling, Health Services, Community Standards, and other campus partners as appropriate. Ensures timely documentation and follow-up regarding significant incidents. Serves as a Campus Security Authority under the Clery Act. Assessment & Departmental Support Assists with assessment of residential programs, student engagement, RA performance, and community-development initiatives. Tracks and reports information related to assigned functional portfolios. Participates in departmental planning and continuous-improvement initiatives. Assists with Orientation, summer operations, University events, and other Residential Life responsibilities. Completes other duties as assigned Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1257P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Bachelors Degree required Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Intermittently sitting, standing, stooping. Light lifting or carrying 25 lbs or less. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8021 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue\r\nWest Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8026": {
      "title": "Manager of Collegiate Budget  &amp; Administration",
      "description": "University of Hartford Employment Site | Manager of Collegiate Budget  &amp; Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Manager of Collegiate Budget  & Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Manager of Collegiate Budget  & Administration FLSA Classification EX Reports to Dean Salary Range F Weeks Per Year 52 Work Week 40 hours (minimum) Position Summary Assumes responsibility for providing leadership and support in the planning, administrative and budgeting operations of the College in an effort to ensure prudent fiscal oversight as well as effective and efficient business operations. Performs all duties in full support of the University’s mission, understanding that the positive and effective execution of these duties are instrumental to the education of the University’s students. Hiring Range Starting Budgeted salary is $50,455 to $55,000, depending upon experience Key Responsibilities Key Responsibilities In collaboration with the Dean and Department Chairs, oversees the development, implementation and maintenance of cost-effective operational approaches to collegiate budget management. Oversees the implementation of short and long-range financial planning initiatives for complex financial, business and administrative services and systems utilized within the College. Prepares detailed statistical and financial reports to be used in the decision-making process. Analyzes complex financial data, making recommendations to the Dean and/or Department Chairs regarding the most cost-effective use of resources. Reviews budgetary projections vs actual operating results, identifying potential discrepancies and proposing possible solutions. Serves as the centralized point for operational expenditures, internal grants and/or personnel transactions within the College. Oversees and maintains budgets, including restricted funds, for the Office of the Dean. Apportions money for anticipated and unanticipated goods and services purchased for departments and the College, initiating and/or approving budget transfers and purchase orders as necessary and/or appropriate. Handles highly sensitive information with confidentiality and tact. Analyzes, monitors and oversees the use of financial, business, fund accounting and administrative services systems across the College. Implements system upgrades and establishes new systems as necessary and/or appropriate. Enforces University and collegiate financial controls, policies and procedures to ensure the integrity of these systems in compliance with established data integrity standards. Actively participates in the analysis, recommendation and implementation of business process improvement efforts to ensure the proper use of technology and improve operational effectiveness as necessary and/or appropriate. Establishes, cultivates and maintains effective working relationships with various internal constituents including, but not limited to, the Provost’s Office, Financial Accounting Services, the Budget Office, Payroll and the Office of Sponsored Programs regarding collegiate financial and budgetary planning and implementation efforts. Performs other related duties as assigned. Posting Detail Information Posting Number PS1259P Working Conditions Normal office situation. Education Bachelor’s Degree Required. Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or table. Special Skills The ability to work effectively with diverse groups. Desired Start Date 11/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Quick Link for Internal Postings https://hartford.peopleadmin.com/postings/8025 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Technical School, Certification or Apprenticeship Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree Knowledge of a highly advanced professional discipline. (e.g., Ph.D, M.D., J.D., or equivalent doctoral degree required.) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation - Staff Statement on Inclusive Excellence and Belonging 200 Bloomfield Avenue West Hartford, CT 06117 Back to top Copyright © 2021 University of Hartford To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
